data: {"id":"gen-1794255515-5IvGKdrF0tOlA9ESHN6W","object":"chat.completion.chunk","created":1794255515,"model":"google/gemini-2.5-flash","provider":"Google AI Studio","choices":[{"index":0,"delta":{"content":"","role":"assistant","reasoning":"**Identifying Environment Issues**\n\nI've examined the latest trace and pinpointed a crucial environment setup error. It seems Chrome is failing to start, resulting in a `SessionNotCreatedException`. The message \"DevToolsActivePort file doesn't exist\" indicates a deeper problem within the Chrome launch sequence. I suspect this stems from Chrome's configuration or a missing dependency, not from an error in the Selenium script itself at this point. I'm focusing on ensuring Chrome is properly installed and that its dependencies are correctly configured within the current setup to address this initialization failure.\n\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"**Identifying Environment Issues**\n\nI've examined the latest trace and pinpointed a crucial environment setup error. It seems Chrome is failing to start, resulting in a `SessionNotCreatedException`. The message \"DevToolsActivePort file doesn't exist\" indicates a deeper problem within the Chrome launch sequence. I suspect this stems from Chrome's configuration or a missing dependency, not from an error in the Selenium script itself at this point. I'm focusing on ensuring Chrome is properly installed and that its dependencies are correctly configured within the current setup to address this initialization failure.\n\n\n","format":"google-gemini-v1","index":0}]},"finish_reason":null,"native_finish_reason":null}]}

